---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "Adult Dog Obedience San Jacinto | Good Doggos";
const description = "Real-world adult dog obedience in San Jacinto. We specialize in building reliable communication and trust through Balanced Clarity, even in high-distraction environments.";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Adult Dog Obedience Training",
  "description": description,
  "provider": {
    "@type": "LocalBusiness",
    "name": "Good Doggos",
    "url": "https://gooddoggos.com",
    "telephone": "+19514016252",
    "address": {
      "@type": "PostalAddress",
      "addressLocality": "San Jacinto",
      "addressRegion": "CA",
      "addressCountry": "US"
    }
  },
  "areaServed": {
    "@type": "AdministrativeArea",
    "name": "Riverside County"
  },
  "url": "https://gooddoggos.com/services/adult-dog-obedience"
};
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(jsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <!-- Hero Band -->
  <section class="bg-primary-navy pt-32 pb-16 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Breadcrumb -->
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-body text-white/50 mt-6 mb-4" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Home</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <a href="/services/pet-trainer" class="text-accent-gold hover:text-accent-gold/80 underline font-semibold">Pet Trainer</a>
        <span>&rsaquo;</span>
        <span class="text-white/80 truncate">Adult Dog Obedience</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-heading font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        Adult Dog Obedience Training in San Jacinto
      </h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Body Content -->
  <section class="py-16 px-4 bg-[#FCF9FA]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose max-w-none">
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          It’s a common misconception that old dogs can't learn new habits. In reality, what most adult dogs are missing isn't the ability to learn, but clear leadership. If you’re being dragged down the sidewalk near Hiram Deville Park or your dog treats your "come" command like a suggestion, these behaviors are symptoms of a lack of clarity.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Because we are professionals, we do not guess or give out generic advice. We must evaluate your dog in person to see where the communication is breaking down before we can help you achieve real-world reliability. Our balanced approach is built on providing you and your dog with high-value rewards and clear boundaries.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-primary-navy mt-12 mb-6">
          Reliability Beyond the Biscuit
        </h2>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          At Good Doggos, we specialize in the "stubborn" adults and dogs that have spent years practicing the wrong behaviors. For over 8 years, I’ve been helping Riverside County owners achieve real-world results. My balanced approach is built on "Balanced Clarity." I use high-value rewards and heavy praise to show your dog what I want, but I also provide well-timed, fair corrections. Like a parent with a child, we nurture good behavior but aren't afraid to set boundaries.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          Take the case of Camila, a reactive Pitbull/Boxer mix. Her previous trainer said she was un-trainable and suggested she be put down. On her very first day with me, she was walking and laying down peacefully next to my helper dog, Simba. This didn't happen by coddling her fear; it happened by giving her a leader she could finally trust.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6">
          We don't train in a vacuum. We take our sessions to the real-world environments of San Jacinto, from the busy intersections of State Street to the distractions at Valley-Wide Regional Park. We work on the fundamentals: a rock-solid "place" command, a "heel" that saves your shoulder, and a recall that works even when the Santa Ana winds are kicking up dust. By the time we’re finished, your dog will be a neutral, reliable companion anywhere in the Inland Empire.
        </p>
        <p class="text-secondary-slate leading-[1.8] font-body text-[16px] mb-6 font-bold">
          If you’re ready to stop making excuses and start making progress, I’m here to help.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA BAND
══════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#FBF1E9]" style="border-top: 1px solid #E6DAC6;">
  <div class="w-full h-[3px]" style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #0F6D72, #D1B27F, #0F6D72);"></div>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-20 md:py-24 text-center">
    <p class="text-[11px] font-bold tracking-[0.25em] uppercase mb-4" style="color: rgba(15,109,114,0.60);">Your Dog Is Next</p>
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4" style="color: #0B2744;">
      Ready to See What's Possible?<br/>
      <span class="headline-accent" style="color: #D1B27F; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700;">Start With a Free Assessment.</span>
    </h2>
    <p class="text-base mb-10 max-w-lg mx-auto" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.60);">
      Tell us about your dog. We'll do an honest assessment and point you toward the right program — or tell you if we're not the right fit.
    </p>
    <a href="/apply"
       class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 font-bold text-sm tracking-widest uppercase rounded-full transition-all duration-200 hover:-translate-y-0.5"
       style="background: #D1B27F; color: #0B2744; padding: 18px 44px; box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(209,178,127,0.35);">
      Apply for Free Behavioral Assessment →
    </a>
    <p class="mt-4 text-xs" style="color: rgba(17,32,50,0.40);">Takes less than 3 minutes · No commitment required</p>
  </div>
</div>
</Layout>
